        StaticItem("Raspberry Scones", "Food: 4\nSaturation: 3.0\nThe rotten food reeks of fungi.", "minecraft:bread", ""),
        StaticItem("Dewlox sized Stakes", "Food: 10\nSaturation: 16.0\nThe rotten food reeks of fungi.", "minecraft:cooked_rabbit", ""),
        StaticItem("Harvest Cake", "A caked baked from the harvests of the season.\nTo enjoy with apple cider or friends.\n*Moderator Approved*\nMorsmordre approved this item.", "minecraft:cake", ""),
        StaticItem("&Tome of Smithing", "you're a shit tier meme, salvo\n★Event Actor Approved★\nSigned by the Donald Drumpf Lord Pepe,\n- Sky-God Overlord", "minecraft:book", ""),
        StaticItem("Lich Horn", "Coltaines Horn", "minecraft:end_rod", ""),
        StaticItem("Ruibrium Tinted Cake", "The cake would be quite delicious, however tinted with\nthe highly addictive Ruibrium, ohmy.\n*Moderator Approved*\nPandann approved this item.", "minecraft:cake", ""),
        StaticItem("Tobacco Roll", "Used to calm down the smoker, making them\nfeel less stressed. Mainly used by soldiers,\nor those suffering through hard times.\nHowever, many use it for personal reasons.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by GusanoArentonio.", "minecraft:paper", ""),
        StaticItem("Maggoty-Fleshy", "What appears to be decayed flesh infested\nwith maggots, purple substance leaking from\nthe many contours of it with each touch as if\nthe skin were a sponge itself. The odor is\nvile and strong, likely capable of causing\nany eyes to shed saline droplets!\n★Event Actor Approved★\nSigned by MisterPapiOfLOTC.", "minecraft:clay_ball", ""),
        StaticItem("Antique Emerald Pendant", "This stunning antique cluster pendant is fine\nquality set with an emerald and very well\ncolour matched, very high colour graded old\ncut diamonds. The pendant is a very good\ngauge of gold and is in excellent condition.", "minecraft:emerald", ""),
        StaticItem("Frost Reaver Skull", "*Moderator Approved*\ni_am_Ricky approved this item.", "minecraft:skull", ""),
        StaticItem("Ruby Tipped Rod", "A Peculiar foot long rod of metal, inscribed\nin the side with strange symbols. A large,\nglowing ruby would rest at the top of it.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Lhindir_.", "minecraft:torch", ""),
        StaticItem("-+- Superior Black-Steel Kiteshield -+-", "A kiteshield wrought in blacksteel, it's\nedges lined in a fine trim of gleaming\nsilver. The shield was not flat, two slopes\nthat would meet together to create an arched\nridge vertically along the center of it.\nInlaid upon the shield would be the crest of\nHouse Horen, a three headed dragon that\ndisplayed itself proudly atop the shield.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by The Blacksmith.", "minecraft:shield", ""),
        StaticItem("Severed Golem Arm", "A battered and worn runic prosthetic lined\nwith deep channels that emits a blue,\nsupernatural glow. Further inspection of the\nrunic limb may allude to the telltale of an\nIrongut's craftsmanship. Blood and dried gore\nstain the edge of the limb with the remains\nof a bone protruding", "minecraft:netherbrick", ""),
        StaticItem("Soul-Bound Item", "Save this for the end of the dungeon to\nrecieve a reward.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by freema5.", "minecraft:ender_eye", ""),
        StaticItem("Fire Runestone", "A surfaced flatstone, round in shape and\nhardened to touch, appears to be held within\nyour hand. Engraved deep into the flat\nsurface would be what seems to be an\nintricately carved rune, one any speaker of\nAncient Dwed or pracitioner of the\nRunesmithing art would recognise as 'Fire\nRune'. Through verbal activation of the\nDwedmar word 'Fire', flames would spur from\nthe surface of the rune.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Crumena Synalli.", "minecraft:stone", ""),
        StaticItem("Snake Rock", "A small, round, smooth rock with the\nengraving of a slim snake curled so that its\nhead touched the end of its tail.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Callwarrior.", "minecraft:cobblestone", ""),
        StaticItem("Silver Spoon", "This spoon is the epitone of fine silversmith\ncraftsmanship. The piece of silverware\nfeatures an intricate, ornate cluster of\nfruit, leaves, and flowers lavishly engraved\ninto its handle, adding unforgetting elegance\nwhen in view.", "minecraft:iron_shovel", ""),
        StaticItem("Wolf Skin", "A pelt from a small wolf, white fur that is\nrather warm to the touch.-et\n★Event Actor Approved★\nSigned by Assassinofawsome.", "minecraft:leather", ""),
        StaticItem("Feather Duster", "An elegant feather duster of white\nfeathers and a black stained wooden\nhandle.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Maidservant.", "minecraft:feather", ""),
        StaticItem("Arcanist Stone", "* A bound Arcanist Stone of Fine quality *\n[Celestial: Balthazar]\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by BrandNewKitten.", "minecraft:nether_wart", ""),
        StaticItem("Sword of Wight Woe", "This black ferrum arming sword is nearly\nidentical to its mundane counterparts, except\nfor the bleached skull which serves as its\ncrossguard, said to have belonged to a man\nwho would go on to become one of the very\nfirst ever Gravens in recorded history.", "minecraft:iron_sword", ""),
        StaticItem("Wings of the Queen of Bats", "This jet black double-headed axe was forged\nfrom blackened steel and Wyvern bone by an\ninfatuated blacksmith upon catching first\nsight of Eleonora, Princess of the\nWesterlands. Each of the twin heads unfurls\nfrom the haft, their respective edges hook\nthrice successively at their ends until\nreaching back, resembling the wings of a\ngiant bat. This unwieldy weapon measures\nnearly 6' in height, making it far too heavy\nto use in battle without quickly exhausting.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by GusanoArentonio.", "minecraft:iron_axe", ""),
        StaticItem("Wraith Shard", "★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Josh3738.", "minecraft:end_stone", ""),
        StaticItem("Monster Hunter License", "This license is granted to Duke Jon Renault\nde Savoie, allowing for the tracking,hunting\nand killing of Monsters. The monster hunter\nis expected to follow The Laws of Monsters\nand Unnatural Anomalies. Signed, Imperial\nHuntsman, Philip de Capua.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Gucko.", "minecraft:paper", ""),
        StaticItem("The Miragecrafter's Crest", "An aged and slightly weathered silver ring bearing\na large purple gemstone mounted over the band of\nsilver. It shimmers a faint purple hue as the emblem\nof the Arcane Delvers can be seen floating within the\nconfines of the gem. The ring legended to belong to\none of the founders of the Arcane Delvers, Polgrath,\nthe first Mind Lord. A relic that was thought to have\nbeen lost during the infamous Magi's sudden\ndisappearance. Upon being donned the ring would\nappear to greatly augment the abilities of an Illusionist.\nYet for some odd reason a grim and rather sinister\npresence would appear to resonate from the accessory.\n*Moderator Approved*\nMysticWalrus approved this item.", "minecraft:emerald", ""),
        StaticItem("Chalice of Wine", "A bitter alcohol of crimson hue within a\nchalice of aurum. It never empties nor does\nthat taste ever disappoint!\n★Event Actor Approved★\nSigned by MisterPapiOfLOTC.", "minecraft:skull", ""),
        StaticItem("Chain of Ogrol (Ilzgûl Udalgum)", "This silver jewellery shimmers in the light,\nyet a darkness is latent within the gem in\nthe centre. After prolonged exposure, the\nwearer would find themselves sapped of\nstrength.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Dohvi.", "minecraft:iron_bars", ""),
        StaticItem("The Stone of the Cognat", "A seemingly ordinary and uneventful stone,\nadorning a soft and gentle glow to the purple\ncloak it appears to bear. Covering the stone\nlike a blanket appears to be a shimmer of\ntight measure, and should one connect to the\nVoid while holding stone in hand, one may\nexperience something truly... interesting.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Crumena Izalith.", "minecraft:obsidian", ""),
        StaticItem("Orb of Xaakt - Ilzgûl Udalgûm", "A sizable orb that lays comfortably in ones\nhand. A black orb, swirling with crimson\ncontents. On the surface of this fist sized,\nashen glass would be shamanic writings,\nengraved upon the weak shell.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by FlamboyantUsopp.", "minecraft:skull", ""),
        StaticItem("Occulist(?)'s Staff", "The staff has a wooden, thin, light shaft,\nwith an iron head shaped like a rose's head.\nThe words \"For my one Evie. - Badu.\" is\ncarved on the wooden shaft, with few spots of\ncrimson red littering the smooth surface. The\nstaff, once yielded by the old necromancer\nEvelangéline now available for its next user,\nin hopes it returns to herself...\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by EdgyMagey.", "minecraft:golden_hoe", ""),
        StaticItem("Delrof's Wroth", "A blood laced brick, it gives of an ominous vibe.\nIt smells of medical herbs from the Northern Region.", "minecraft:brick", ""),
        StaticItem("Everlasting Candle", "A sweet aura escapes the formed wax that sits\nwithin a candle holder of plenty details. The\nwick obtains a mere flame that seems to never\ndie out no matter what absurd impacts it is\ngranted\n★Event Actor Approved★\nSigned by MisterPapiOfLOTC.", "minecraft:skull", ""),
        StaticItem("The Timekeeper‘s Call", "Magic V\nEnlightenment II\nSoulbind I\nAn impressive staff composed entirely of glistening\nCarbarum. The staff resonates an aura of absolute\nwisdom. Numerous numerals and Arcane-like-icons\nline the shaft of the mighty staff. Shimmering with a\nperception of sagacity. At the very tip of the staff lay\ntwo arrows; one long and narrow and one half as\nlong as it's larger companion, crossing over one\nanother and pointing upward. Appearing rather\nsimilar to that of a clock's hands striking twelve.\n*Moderator Approved*\nDizzy771 approved this item.", "minecraft:diamond_hoe", ""),
        StaticItem("The Timekeeper’s Chrono", "Seeking VII\nKnowledge V\nAncient II\nA constellation of stars and runes dot the the edge of this\ngolden pocket watch, telling time is impossible with it as\nthe arms never function as suspected. It was once called\nthe Seeker's Compass. A blessed tool of Xan's used to\nfind those worthy of joining the ranks of the Order of the\nGolden Lance. After Setherien's demise the watch appears\nto have taken on a new purpose; to whoever holds the watch\nthe urge to protect the vulnerable encompasses it's owner.\nFlaring with a crisp sapphire glow when near large quantities\nof corruption and taint. Always tugging to the site of such\nunholy occurrences. It should also be noted that an icon of\na lance is proudly engraved on the lid of the watch.", "minecraft:clock", ""),
