        StaticItem("Daydreamer", "A briljant wooden craft standing at about 5\nft tall. The tip is curved to a circle where\na webbing is spun to fill the formed circle.\nBeads and feathers find themselves entangled\nwith the mandala shaped dreamcatcher. The\nlower end is carved into a sharp point. These\ndecorations fit the name of both staff and\nwielder 'daydreamer\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by HedgeHug.", "minecraft:wooden_hoe", ""),
        StaticItem("Arm of the First Enchanter", "The steel arm was forged from what looks like\nmagic, being perfect and reforged to be light\nweight yet durable. The arm has three\nhatches, one by the shoulder, one in the\nmiddle of the arm, and one at the wrist,\nthese hatches hide diamond gemstones that\npower the arm. A runic mark would be placed\non each hatch, glowing gently in a neon-green\ncolor when the arm is chargedm they don't\nhave any use besides look. The arms gems must\nbe refilled every 5 years (5weeksirl).\n★Magic Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Toodles.", "minecraft:iron_ingot", ""),
        StaticItem("Leg of the First Enchanter", "The metal leg has been forged through a feat\nof magic, the steel being perfectly light yet\ndurable. The leg has three hatches on it, one\nlocated at the top back of the upper thigh,\none in the lower back of the thigh, and one\nin the middle of of the calf. Each hatch\nwould have a rune on it that would glow in a\nbright green glow when the leg is charged,\nthough they serve no use. The legs mana gems\nmust be refilled every 5 years (5weeks irl).\nThe leg functions like a normal leg, even in\ncombat.\n★Magic Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Toodles.", "minecraft:iron_ingot", ""),
