        StaticItem("❃ Flowing Elegant Dress ❃", "Arcane I\nA violet dress with golden hues decorating\nits edges, suitable to be worn by any\nmedium-sized creature such as the average\nhuman or elf. If looked at long enough one\ncould notice a very faint sheen of light\ncross over its fabric. Should this be attuned\nto you by the appropriate method, wearing the\ndress will cast a glamor of a beautiful young\nblonde woman over your existing features.\nThis slowly drains your energy until you die\nor remove the dress. [PM Gladuos for details]\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Gladuos.", "minecraft:leather_chestplate", ""),
        StaticItem("Ruhn oz Wuglim", "The small stone is flat enough on one side to\ncarry a small rune. At the mention of the\nword of activation, Wuglim, the rune begins\nto glow softly and water would begin to flow\nsteadily from the surface of the rune until\nthe activation word is repeated. The rune\nitself, as all runes do, would wear out after\nan extended period without renewal and would\nlikely stop working after 4 or 5 uses.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Josh3738.", "minecraft:stone", ""),
        StaticItem("Ponderlot", "This is a handful of powdered ponderlot\npetals. It is a potent depressant and\nhallucinogen. On consumption, it induces\neuphoria and passivity, with most sense\nheightened or distorted. It may be smoked, or\neaten orally, the latter producing a briefer\nbut more intense high. Traditionally, it's\nused by druids or dedicants who seek a closer\nconnection to nature.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Z3m0s.", "minecraft:dye", ""),
        StaticItem("House Serene Pendant", "A masterful crafted pendant made entirely of\nemerald except a outline around it would be\nmade from a golden trim. On this pendant can\nbe seen that a Blue orchid has been chiseled\nout of a blue sapphire and was embedded in\nthe pendant. The Blue orchid made to\nrepresent the undying and most cultured House\nSerene.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Bolon Stormtaker.", "minecraft:emerald", ""),
        StaticItem("Bees that Listen", "This is a butterfly wing bottle containing\nsixteen yellowthorn bees. Their stings are\nmildly painful and cause minor swelling, but\nare not lethal and do not have systemic\neffects. When the bottle containing them is\nopened or shattered, they may be given a\nsingle command, which they will follow to the\nbest of their ability. They perish one\nSaint's half-hour after being released.\n★Game Moderator Approved★\nSigned by Z3m0s.", "minecraft:glass_bottle", ""),
        StaticItem("Ironwood Sword", "An ironwood blade reaching two and a half\nfeet in length. Silver, with a faded red hue.\nCurving gently upward, it would mimic a\nswerving snake near its tip. A spiral pattern\nnavigating down both sides of the blade. Its\nhilt would be comprised of an ashen wood,\nvines, bear leather, and a hexagonal emerald\nin the center of the cross-guard.", "minecraft:iron_sword", ""),
        StaticItem("The Seer's Candle", "A smooth white candle with hints of\nopalescent tints that exudes an aroma like\nthat of an incense.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by ski_king3.", "minecraft:skull", ""),
        StaticItem("Bamboo Panflute", "A well-made panflute, composed of\nthick bamboo segments held together\nby wool string. If treated well, it will\nlast for a long time.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Roxforbraynz.", "minecraft:reeds", ""),
        StaticItem("Haensetian Wayfinder", "A semi clear gem seeming to thrum with\nmagical energy, when tapped thrice it emits a\nbright light around the user, lighting their\nway in darkness.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by HurferDurfer.", "minecraft:prismarine_shard", ""),
        StaticItem("fat monkey poster", "★Player Approved★\nSigned by jhon_boat.", "minecraft:sign", ""),
        StaticItem("Elderwood Crown", "A crown formed of elderwood, looped and\ntwisted together as if the wood were thread.\nCresting the face would be arches- shaped to\nresemble a tree canopy. Three oval emeralds,\noutlined with the designs of twirling vines\namongst the leaves. A pair of branching\nantlers in the wood splitting them equally\napart, intersecting along the rim. An\nintricate, treeline-like pattern tracing the\ncrown around, never overlapping. Some trunks\nsprouting skyward to support a ceiling of\nleaves.\n★Player Approved★\nSigned by Guyden.", "minecraft:leather_helmet", ""),
